This article is about one of the largest known meat-eating dinosaurs, and therefore one of the largest terrestrial carnivores to have ever existed. The dinosaur is thought to have equalled or even surpassed ''[[Tyrannosaurus]]'' in length, and the article is one of the most viewed dinosaur articles on Wikipedia. The article contains practically everything ever published about this animal, and covers the scientific debate/competition about the maximum size of theropod dinosaurs. The article is a GA and has been copy-edited. [[User:FunkMonk|FunkMonk]] ([[User talk:FunkMonk|talk]]) 17:10, 30 September 2016 (UTC)
====Comments from Jim====
Very comprehensive and well written, but, of course, some quibbles
